{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788161285,"nonce":"DxY3TXZu6wfcy7jgKCFyt34fXu0=","title":"ci: no path filter on `ci.yml` — an art-only push runs the full Rust suite twice","message":"`ci.yml` has no `paths:` filter at any level. Every push to any PR — and every\npush to main — runs `test`, `coverage`, `ui-tests`, `ui-unit`, `ui-e2e` and\n`openapi-drift`, whatever changed.\n\nMeasured on PR #3 (only `ui/**` and one shell script changed): **26.9 runner-\nminutes across 15 jobs**, of which the Rust suite twice (18.2 min) and\n`openapi-drift` (0.8 min) could not possibly have been affected.\n\n`kind.yml` already does this correctly — it path-filters to the crates it\nexercises, which is exactly why `kind/cluster-tests` was the one job that\ncorrectly sat out PR #3.\n\nThe mechanism is already in the repo and needs no invention:\n`.github/required-checks.txt` defines a `required-if-run` tier, documented there\nas being for \"PATH-FILTERED jobs, whose absence is correct on an unrelated PR\",\nand `scripts/pr_gate.py` implements it (prints \"skipped (path filter) — OK\").\n\nShape:\n\n* a `changes` job (e.g. `dorny/paths-filter`) emitting `rust` / `ui` / `api`;\n* each job gated on the relevant output;\n* the newly-skippable checks moved from `required` to `required-if-run` in\n  `.github/required-checks.txt`.\n\nExpected: a UI-only PR drops from ~27 min / 15 jobs to roughly 1 min / 3 jobs.\nA Rust PR is unchanged and still fully gated.\n\nCare needed on the boundary cases — `Cargo.lock`, `openapi.json`, the workflow\nfiles themselves, and anything the server image embeds — should all count as\n`rust`/`api` so a filter can never hide a real break.","files":null}]}